    {
      "id": "m17",
      "question": "How can I tell if an MCP server changed a tool's definition after I approved it?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T20:00:44.679Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Store a baseline fingerprint when you first review and approve the MCP tools. `fingerprintTools` digests each tool’s description, resolved input schema, and title into a stable map keyed by tool name. [1: \"`fingerprintTools` digests the server-controlled, security-relevant fields of each tool\"]\n\nOn later fetches, fingerprint the tools again and compare the new map with the baseline using `detectToolDrift`. Check its `changed` and `added` results; if either is non-empty, block use of the tools, require re-approval, or alert before passing them to the model. [1: \"`detectToolDrift` diffs two such maps\"] [1: \"Block, re-approve, or alert per your policy\"]\n\nYour app must store the baseline and decide how to respond; the SDK does not persist baselines or block calls. This detects changes to descriptions, input schemas, and titles, but not a remote behavior or endpoint swap when those fields remain unchanged. [1: \"Core stays unopinionated: it does not persist baselines or block calls\"] [1: \"It cannot detect a behavior/endpoint swap\"]",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "citation",
          "n": 1,
          "quote": "`fingerprintTools` digests the server-controlled, security-relevant fields of each tool",
          "status": "verified"
        },
        {
          "type": "citation",
          "n": 1,
          "quote": "`detectToolDrift` diffs two such maps",
          "status": "verified"
        },
        {
          "type": "citation",
          "n": 1,
          "quote": "Block, re-approve, or alert per your policy",
          "status": "not-found"
        },
        {
          "type": "citation",
          "n": 1,
          "quote": "Core stays unopinionated: it does not persist baselines or block calls",
          "status": "verified"
        },
        {
          "type": "citation",
          "n": 1,
          "quote": "It cannot detect a behavior/endpoint swap",
          "status": "verified"
        }
      ],
