      "id": "m18",
      "question": "How do I handle an MCP server that asks the user for more input during a tool call?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T20:00:48.752Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Advertise elicitation support when creating the MCP client by setting `capabilities: { elicitation: {} }`. [1: \"To enable elicitation, you need to advertise the capability when creating the MCP client\"] Register an `onElicitationRequest` handler to receive the server’s request; it includes a message and a schema describing the expected input. [1: \"Use the `onElicitationRequest` method to register a handler that will be called when the server requests input\"] In the handler, collect the input in a way appropriate to your application, then return an action: `accept` with `content` containing the supplied data, `decline` if the user refuses, or `cancel` if they cancel the operation. [1: \"Your handler must return an object with an `action` field that can be one of\"] The MCP client surfaces requests to your application; the client itself does not handle them for you. [1: \"The MCP client simply surfaces these requests from the server to your application code\"]",
