      "question": "How do I let the model discover tools on demand instead of sending all of them?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T20:00:59.619Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Set tools you want to defer to `deferLoading: true`, then register `toolSearch()` in the `tools` object. The model initially sees only the search tool; after searching, matching tool definitions are added and the model can call them directly. [5: \"The model initially sees only `search`. After searching, matching definitions are added to the provider's tool list\"]\n\nYou can use this with `generateText`, `streamText`, `ToolLoopAgent`, or `WorkflowAgent`; `toolSearch()` takes no arguments because the model supplies the search query. [1: \"`toolSearch()` lets a model find the tools it needs without loading every tool's definition into its initial context\"] Discovered tools are available for the rest of that generation. [4: \"keeps discovered tools available for the rest of the generation\"]",
